      "writtenOn": "2023-05-30T19:59:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can all be handled in userspace, there\u0027s no need for any kernel changes at all.  It was solved back in the 2.6 days with persistent device naming done by userspace based on the information exported in sysfs.",
      "revId": "2a60ff89d36e6ffefec3b1af3fffe5131ba7ed56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83288324_94053023",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2005211
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T01:21:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I don\u0027t understand your comment. I assume that it could be solved by userspace but I have no idea. Could you please tell me how to solve it?",
      "parentUuid": "94c2cafd_612c76e6",
      "revId": "2a60ff89d36e6ffefec3b1af3fffe5131ba7ed56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "552efc9a_352a6e98",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T15:06:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "USB device ids and bus numbers should NEVER expect to be the same across boots, or even over time on the same machine without rebooting (devices can come and go).\n\nWhat matters is how userspace accesses these devices, and it does so using names picked by userspace depending on lots of different things (topology, serial numbers, partition names, etc.)  Use that in userspace, the kernel does not care here at all.\n\nThis was 1/2 of the reason that Linux adopted a unified driver/device model 18+ years ago.  This isn\u0027t new at all 😊\n\nFor more details, you can always look up the old papers published about `udev` for one example of how to do this.  Also look at your desktop system in /dev/disk/ for examples of how your Linux desktop system handles this today.",
      "parentUuid": "83288324_94053023",
      "revId": "2a60ff89d36e6ffefec3b1af3fffe5131ba7ed56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a6b1d78_21377c92",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2005211
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T04:46:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t expect it for USB device ids. That could be checked by lots of different things as you said. But for bus number, if it\u0027s changed, this means the change of topology for USB bus.\nAnd regarding to any other serial bus supported by Linux (e.g. i2c,spi,serial,etc.), these driver support fixed bus number by alias id.\nSo I think that it\u0027s applicable to usb.\n\nI have experienced same issue for long time in IVI system that is based on udev.\nIt\u0027s difficult to solve it by using udev.\nRegarding to /dev/disk, it\u0027s slightly different from bus id\u0027s case.",
      "parentUuid": "552efc9a_352a6e98",
      "revId": "2a60ff89d36e6ffefec3b1af3fffe5131ba7ed56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5eb36e31_e5c23f0e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T06:34:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "USB bus ids are even more random than device ids, as you have found out.  They are not deterministic at all, and in fact, can change at any time, as you have found out.\n\nYou should NEVER rely on them to be the same.\n\nLook at the device attributes instead, to determine what you need to communicate with, USB bus numbers are only guaranteed to be unique at a specific point in time (i.e. no two busses have the same number), but the actual number is never guaranteed to be a specific value.",
      "parentUuid": "5a6b1d78_21377c92",
      "revId": "2a60ff89d36e6ffefec3b1af3fffe5131ba7ed56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e3b4bec_7c5d6d8b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2005211
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T09:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand you.\nI\u0027d like to back to first point.\nUSB bus ids are random, I know it caused some issue in IVI system for long time.\nIt\u0027s difficult to avoid by userspace.\nTo prevent from being random ids, I\u0027ve submit this patch so that we can fix and consist bus ids by device alias. If no alias specified, it\u0027s compatible.\nWe have fixed the issue like that for long time. we don\u0027t have any other solution now.",
      "parentUuid": "5eb36e31_e5c23f0e",
      "revId": "2a60ff89d36e6ffefec3b1af3fffe5131ba7ed56",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
